 "template": "In Odoo, go to the Sales app and create a new quotation. Set the Customer field to '{{v1}}' — it is an autocomplete dropdown, so type the name and actually select the option from the dropdown list that appears (do not just type it). Then in the Order Lines table, add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (again via the autocomplete dropdown, selecting an actual option), and set its Quantity to 3. Let the app auto-fill the unit price. Do NOT confirm the quotation — leave it as a draft quotation. Save the quotation. Then report: (a) the exact product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that line, (c) the Untaxed Amount the app computes, and (d) the quotation's reference/name shown in the breadcrumb or form header. Do not wait for network idle (the app long-polls); wait for concrete page state instead.",
